  "log": [
    "====================================================================================================",
    "DO THESE TWO PROTEINS INTERACT AT ALL? -- the question that does not need pose ranking solved",
    "====================================================================================================",
    "  Dock-then-score is blocked: the top pose is rank ~1,791 of 9,600, so it scores a wrong structure.",
    "  But WHETHER they bind can be read from the pose-score DISTRIBUTION without knowing WHERE.",
    "  PAIRED design: every receptor appears once with its true partner and once with a size-matched",
    "  foreign chain, so per-protein effects cancel. Features are z-scored WITHIN each pair, so raw",
    "  magnitude (which tracks size) cannot reach the classifier.",
    "  PREDECLARED: beats size_only AND label_perm => detection works where ranking does not.",
    "  ~ size_only => it learned protein size. ~ label_perm => nothing at all.",
    "\n  80 usable complexes; building 40 paired examples",
    "    10 docked (388s)",
    "    20 docked (605s)",
    "    30 docked (830s)",
    "    40 docked (1040s)",
    "    50 docked (1254s)",
    "    60 docked (1485s)",
    "    70 docked (1718s)",
    "    80 docked (1947s)",
    "\n  80 docked runs | 40 positive, 40 negative | 40 distinct receptors",
    "  receptors appearing in BOTH classes (the paired design): 40",
    "\n  arm                    AUC   (GroupKFold by receptor, so no receptor spans train and test)",
    "  docking dist         0.456",
    "  size_only            0.438   <- the artefact baseline",
    "  label_perm           0.496   median of 200, 95th 0.636",
    "  chance               0.500",
    "  permutation p = 0.6600",
    "\n  READING",
    "  IT LEARNED SIZE. docking 0.456 vs size_only 0.438 -- the distribution",
    "  features add nothing over how big the two chains are, despite per-pair z-scoring. The paired",
    "  design and the size arm are exactly what make that visible rather than flattering."
  ]
